WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.669
Cedar Vale Foods buys solar support and

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.523
battery monitoring from Beacon Grid.

00:00:04.773 --> 00:00:06.586
One customer, two services.

00:00:06.836 --> 00:00:09.034
Where should each agreement's terms, sales

00:00:09.034 --> 00:00:11.529
history and billing evidence live in HubSpot?

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.748
We'll follow solar support, compare battery

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:16.898
monitoring, and build a map you can use

00:00:16.898 --> 00:00:17.896
on your own records.

00:00:18.146 --> 00:00:20.514
The HubSpot screens show prepared drafts.

00:00:20.764 --> 00:00:23.362
The documents are illustrations, not signed

00:00:23.362 --> 00:00:23.964
agreements.

00:00:24.633 --> 00:00:26.877
Solar support runs from November twenty

00:00:26.877 --> 00:00:28.827
twenty-six through October twenty

00:00:28.827 --> 00:00:29.540
twenty-seven.

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:32.091
Battery monitoring starts and ends a month

00:00:32.091 --> 00:00:32.499
later.

00:00:32.749 --> 00:00:35.122
Each has its own service scope and renewal

00:00:35.122 --> 00:00:35.715
decision.

00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:38.239
That's why we give them separate agreement

00:00:38.239 --> 00:00:39.012
identities.

00:00:39.262 --> 00:00:41.213
It isn't a rule of one Contract per

00:00:41.213 --> 00:00:41.822
product.

00:00:42.072 --> 00:00:44.891
Services managed under one set of terms can

00:00:44.891 --> 00:00:47.213
share a Contract with several line items.

00:00:47.867 --> 00:00:50.085
The Company identifies the customer.

00:00:50.335 --> 00:00:52.733
It cannot, by itself, tell you which service

00:00:52.733 --> 00:00:54.837
an end date or a price belongs to.

00:00:55.087 --> 00:00:57.231
Keep those facts connected to the specific

00:00:57.231 --> 00:00:57.775
agreement.

00:00:58.433 --> 00:01:00.140
Start with the legal evidence.

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:02.913
The master agreement, service schedule and

00:01:02.913 --> 00:01:05.013
accepted amendments establish what the

00:01:05.013 --> 00:01:06.001
parties agreed.

00:01:06.251 --> 00:01:08.720
HubSpot's commercial Contract does not

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:10.091
replace those documents.

00:01:10.767 --> 00:01:13.064
Next, the Deal answers: which sales

00:01:13.064 --> 00:01:14.628
opportunity are we working on?

00:01:14.878 --> 00:01:17.047
Here, the solar draft links to its source

00:01:17.047 --> 00:01:17.417
Deal.

00:01:17.667 --> 00:01:20.189
A future renewal opportunity has a different

00:01:20.189 --> 00:01:21.912
job from the original sale.

00:01:22.567 --> 00:01:24.589
A Quote presents a proposal for buyer

00:01:24.589 --> 00:01:26.833
acceptance, when that route is used.

00:01:27.083 --> 00:01:28.927
Accepted HubSpot quotes can create

00:01:28.927 --> 00:01:29.686
Contracts.

00:01:29.936 --> 00:01:32.059
An agreement signed elsewhere can instead

00:01:32.059 --> 00:01:34.384
be recorded through the direct-create route,

00:01:34.384 --> 00:01:35.163
when available.

00:01:35.833 --> 00:01:38.727
The commercial Contract holds the services,

00:01:38.727 --> 00:01:40.911
term and committed revenue being managed.

00:01:41.161 --> 00:01:43.608
This solar example is still a draft, so

00:01:43.608 --> 00:01:44.958
its values are proposed.

00:01:45.208 --> 00:01:47.981
A populated record is not proof of customer

00:01:47.981 --> 00:01:48.728
acceptance.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:51.320
The invoice answers what was billed.

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:53.789
The payment record shows payment activity

00:01:53.789 --> 00:01:54.514
and status.

00:01:54.764 --> 00:01:57.409
For this example, HubSpot billing stays off.

00:01:57.659 --> 00:01:59.711
We have not created invoices or

00:01:59.711 --> 00:02:01.158
demonstrated collections.

00:02:01.833 --> 00:02:04.031
A Subscription needs one extra check.

00:02:04.281 --> 00:02:06.678
In the standard billing flow, it can manage

00:02:06.678 --> 00:02:07.587
recurring billing.

00:02:07.837 --> 00:02:10.289
In a connected billing setup, it can support

00:02:10.289 --> 00:02:12.680
reporting while the Contract controls billing.

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:15.403
Check which setup your account uses before

00:02:15.403 --> 00:02:17.133
deciding where to make changes.

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:19.123
Now check the numbers.

00:02:19.373 --> 00:02:21.845
The solar line is one thousand US dollars

00:02:21.845 --> 00:02:24.045
per month, quantity one, for twelve

00:02:24.045 --> 00:02:24.621
payments.

00:02:24.871 --> 00:02:27.143
That gives twelve thousand dollars across this

00:02:27.143 --> 00:02:27.836
fixed term.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:30.612
Those numbers describe different measures.

00:02:30.862 --> 00:02:33.213
The monthly recurring price is one thousand

00:02:33.213 --> 00:02:33.742
dollars.

00:02:33.992 --> 00:02:35.933
The term total is twelve thousand.

00:02:36.183 --> 00:02:38.631
Neither tells you how much has been invoiced

00:02:38.631 --> 00:02:39.234
or paid.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:42.298
If a fifteen-hundred-dollar commissioning fee

00:02:42.298 --> 00:02:44.873
belongs to the same agreement, it adds to

00:02:44.873 --> 00:02:47.198
the total commitment, not the recurring

00:02:47.198 --> 00:02:48.135
monthly price.

00:02:48.385 --> 00:02:50.407
If it is separate, leave it outside the

00:02:50.407 --> 00:02:51.307
solar agreement.

00:02:51.557 --> 00:02:54.259
Don't carry a one-time fee into recurring

00:02:54.259 --> 00:02:55.291
renewal charges.

00:02:55.967 --> 00:02:57.887
Always name the field you're comparing.

00:02:58.137 --> 00:03:00.659
Deal Amount, recurring value and Contract

00:03:00.659 --> 00:03:03.129
total can have different calculation rules.

00:03:03.379 --> 00:03:05.973
Check the line items and term that produced

00:03:05.973 --> 00:03:06.963
the displayed number.

00:03:07.633 --> 00:03:09.760
Battery monitoring follows the same

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:10.876
responsibility map.

00:03:11.126 --> 00:03:13.749
It's two hundred and fifty dollars monthly for

00:03:13.749 --> 00:03:16.199
twelve payments: three thousand dollars

00:03:16.199 --> 00:03:17.142
across its term.

00:03:17.392 --> 00:03:19.840
Its end date is November thirtieth, twenty

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:20.592
twenty-seven.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.911
The customer is shared, but the evidence,

00:03:23.911 --> 00:03:26.311
terms and next action must point to battery

00:03:26.311 --> 00:03:26.941
monitoring.

00:03:27.191 --> 00:03:29.539
A link through the same Company is not

00:03:29.539 --> 00:03:31.564
enough to prove that an invoice or a

00:03:31.564 --> 00:03:33.485
Deal belongs to that agreement.

00:03:34.167 --> 00:03:36.589
Associations also don't guarantee

00:03:36.589 --> 00:03:37.473
synchronization.

00:03:37.723 --> 00:03:40.717
HubSpot can copy line items into separate

00:03:40.717 --> 00:03:41.734
record instances.

00:03:41.984 --> 00:03:44.457
Compare their values and parent records,

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:46.832
rather than assuming one edit updates every

00:03:46.832 --> 00:03:47.573
linked record.

00:03:48.233 --> 00:03:49.684
Here's the completed map.

00:03:49.934 --> 00:03:52.153
The Company identifies the customer.

00:03:52.403 --> 00:03:54.323
Documents supply agreed terms.

00:03:54.573 --> 00:03:56.087
Deals track opportunities.

00:03:56.337 --> 00:03:57.809
Quotes present proposals.

00:03:58.059 --> 00:04:00.235
Contracts manage commercial commitments.

00:04:00.485 --> 00:04:02.687
Billing records show charges and payment

00:04:02.687 --> 00:04:04.773
activity, according to your setup.

00:04:05.433 --> 00:04:07.902
Here's one example row for the companion

00:04:07.902 --> 00:04:08.463
workbook.

00:04:08.713 --> 00:04:11.260
The proposed service end is the thirty-first of

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:13.150
October, twenty twenty-seven.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:16.148
Its source is Solar Support Proposal, version

00:04:16.148 --> 00:04:18.673
one, and its record is the Solar Support

00:04:18.673 --> 00:04:19.181
draft.

00:04:19.431 --> 00:04:21.351
In this example, the dates match.

00:04:21.601 --> 00:04:24.570
Sales Ops' next action is to request internal

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:25.057
review.

00:04:25.307 --> 00:04:27.501
For your own agreement, record what you

00:04:27.501 --> 00:04:29.702
actually checked and any discrepancy.

00:04:30.367 --> 00:04:31.668
Then make three checks.

00:04:31.918 --> 00:04:33.666
Can you retrieve the correct agreement

00:04:33.666 --> 00:04:34.286
evidence?

00:04:34.536 --> 00:04:36.328
Do the prices and dates match it?

00:04:36.578 --> 00:04:38.876
Do the linked Deal and billing records belong

00:04:38.876 --> 00:04:39.714
to this agreement?

00:04:39.964 --> 00:04:42.439
Record discrepancies and assign an owner.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:45.273
You can start with a shared spreadsheet,

00:04:45.273 --> 00:04:47.323
controlled document links and assigned

00:04:47.323 --> 00:04:48.455
HubSpot tasks.

00:04:48.705 --> 00:04:51.277
Check which Contract creation, quote and

00:04:51.277 --> 00:04:53.777
workflow features your account includes, then

00:04:53.777 --> 00:04:55.851
choose the setup that fits your process.

00:04:56.533 --> 00:04:58.360
Use the accompanying worksheet and

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:01.260
matching architecture guide to map one real

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:01.824
agreement.

00:05:02.074 --> 00:05:04.372
Before automating, know where each fact

00:05:04.372 --> 00:05:06.822
comes from, which record owns it, and who

00:05:06.822 --> 00:05:07.813
will keep it correct.
